tes around unsafe FFI uses. Extensive unit tests added.|\n|**Zig C-ABI adapter & embed exports** <br> `zig/src/c_adapter.zig`, `zig/src/exports_embed.zig`|Exposes new C ABI functions for similarity, jaccard, entity-hash extraction, normalization/quantize de/quantize, and full embedding-index C API (create/destroy/add/search/count/dimensions) with input validation and C-style error codes.|\n|**Zig shared SIMD implementations** <br> `zig/src/shared/similarity.zig`, `zig/src/shared/entities.zig`, `zig/src/shared/normalize.zig`, `zig/src/shared/quantize.zig`, `zig/src/shared/embeddings.zig`|Implements SIMD-accelerated kernels (cosine, Jaccard delegations, entity hashing SIMD path, L2 normalization SIMD, Q4_0 quantize/dequantize) and an in-memory EmbeddingIndex with brute-force top-K search and tests.|\n|**Zig scalar/reference modules & tests** <br> `zig/src/reference/similarity_ref.zig`, `zig/src/reference/entities_ref.zig`, `zig/src/reference/normalize_ref.zig`, `zig/src/reference/quantize_ref.zig`|Adds scalar reference implementations and tests (FNV-1a hashing, tokenization, scalar normalize, Q4_0 reference quantize/dequantize) used for parity and fallback paths.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Rust as Rust code\n    participant FFI as C-ABI boundary (c_adapter)\n    participant Zig as Zig embedding index\n    participant Alloc as Allocator\n\n    Rust->>FFI: zig_embedding_index_create(dims)\n    FFI->>Zig: allocate index (comptime/imports -> EmbeddingIndex.init)\n    Zig->>Alloc: request memory\n    Alloc-->>Zig: memory handle\n    Zig-->>Rust: opaque handle\n\n    Rust->>FFI: zig_embedding_index_add(handle,id,embedding)\n    FFI->>Zig: validate inputs, copy id/vector\n    Zig->>Alloc: allocate id/vector storage\n    Alloc-->>Zig: memory\n    Zig-->>Rust: status code\n\n    Rust->>FFI: zig_embedding_index_search(handle,query,k)\n    FFI->>Zig: validate, compute cosine against entries\n    Zig->>Zig: brute-force top-K selection\n    Zig-->>Rust: write result_ids, scores, written count\n\n    Rust->>FFI: zig_embedding_index_destroy(handle)\n    FFI->>Zig: free entries\n    Zig->>Alloc: deallocate memory\n    Zig-->>Rust: done\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- **sethyanow/markymark#15** — Extends Zig/Rust FFI scaffold; directly related to the implemented Zig kernels and Rust wrappers in this PR.  \n- **sethyanow/markymark#14** — Modifies same markymark-kernels and Zig FFI surface; related scaffold/work that this PR completes.\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 Hop-hop, I coded kernels bold and spry,  \n> > Zig hums, Rust hugs safety as they fly,  \n> > Words hashed, vectors quantized in clover,  \n> > Top-K leaps home — no memory left over,  \n> > A rabbit cheers: “FFI magic, hop forever!”\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 4</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (4 passed)</summary>\n\n|        Check name        | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                       |\n| :----------------------: | :------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|     Description Check    | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                       |\n|        Title check       | ✅ Passed | The title 'feat(brza): Zig SIMD kernels + Rust FFI for markymark' clearly summarizes the main changes: adding SIMD-accelerated Zig kernels and Rust FFI wrappers. |\n|    Docstring Coverage    | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.             