    "body": "<h3>Greptile Summary</h3>\n\nThis PR implements a complete Zig SIMD kernel layer with Rust FFI wrappers for the markymark project. The implementation adds 7 SIMD-accelerated kernels for markdown scanning operations and ports 4 shared kernels from forge BRZA for embedding operations.\n\n## Key Changes\n\n- **Rust FFI Wrappers** (`markymark-kernels/src/`): Safe Rust APIs wrapping Zig kernels with comprehensive error handling, automatic resource cleanup via `Drop`, and extensive test coverage. The `EmbeddingIndex` properly uses `PhantomData<*mut ()>` to prevent `Send`/`Sync` since the underlying Zig allocator is not thread-safe.\n\n- **Zig C ABI Layer** (`zig/src/c_adapter.zig`, `exports_embed.zig`): Well-designed FFI boundary with proper null checking, buffer overflow protection, and clear error codes. The embedding exports use stack allocation optimization for small K values (≤256) to avoid heap allocation overhead.\n\n- **SIMD Implementations** (`zig/src/shared/`): Clean SIMD kernels using `@Vector(4, f32)` for cosine similarity and normalization, with f64 accumulation for numerical stability. The implementations properly fall back to scalar reference code for short vectors.\n\n- **Reference Implementations** (`zig/src/reference/`): Scalar reference implementations for testing SIMD parity and handling edge cases.\n\n## Architecture Quality\n\nThe code demonstrates excellent software engineering practices:\n- Clear separation between SIMD and scalar paths\n- Comprehensive test coverage (90+ Rust tests, 220+ Zig tests)\n- Proper memory management with no leaks\n- Safe FFI boundaries with validation at every layer\n- f64 intermediate precision in SIMD paths to prevent accumulation errors\n\n<h3>Confidence Score: 5/5</h3>\n\n- This PR is safe to merge with minimal risk\n- All FFI boundaries have proper safety documentation, comprehensive tests pass, memory management is sound with Drop implementations, SIMD code includes scalar fallbacks and reference parity tests, and there are no unwraps outside test code\n- No files require special attention\n\n<h3>Important Files Changed</h3>\n\n\n\n\n| Filename | Overview |\n|----------|----------|\n| markymark-kernels/src/embed.rs | Implements safe Rust wrapper for Zig embedding index FFI with proper error handling, Drop cleanup, and comprehensive tests |\n| markymark-kernels/src/hash.rs | FNV-1a entity hash extraction with automatic buffer retry logic and proper error handling |\n| markymark-kernels/src/similarity.rs | Cosine and Jaccard similarity wrappers with input validation and sentinel value checking |\n| zig/src/c_adapter.zig | C ABI exports for markdown scanning kernels with proper null checks and buffer overflow protection |\n| zig/src/exports_embed.zig | Embedding index FFI layer with proper handle casting, stack-based optimization for small K values, and allocation safety |\n| zig/src/shared/embeddings.zig | Brute-force embedding index with proper deduplication, insertion-sort top-K, and comprehensive tests |\n| zig/src/shared/similarity.zig | SIMD cosine similarity with f64 accumulation for numerical stability and fallback to scalar for short vectors |\n| zig/src/shared/entities.zig | SIMD entity hash extraction with whitespace boundary detection and punctuation splitting |\n| zig/src/shared/quantize.zig | Q4_0 quantization/dequantization with SIMD absmax finding and nibble packing |\n| zig/src/shared/normalize.zig | L2 normalization with SIMD sum-of-squares and scaling, with zero vector detection |\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<h3>Flowchart</h3>\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Rust markymark-kernels crate] --> B[FFI Boundary]\n    B --> C[Zig c_adapter.zig exports]\n    B --> D[Zig exports_embed.zig]\n    \n    C --> E[Zig SIMD Kernels]\n    D --> F[Zig Embedding Index]\n    \n    E --> G[heading_scan.zig]\n    E --> H[link_scan.zig]\n    E --> I[tag_scan.zig]\n    E --> J[block_scan.zig]\n    E --> K[token_estimate.zig]\n    E --> L[content_hash.zig]\n    \n    F --> M[shared/embeddings.zig]\n    M --> N[shared/similarity.zig]\n    \n    C --> O[Shared Kernels]\n    O --> N\n    O --> P[shared/entities.zig]\n    O --> Q[shared/normalize.zig]\n    O --> R[shared/quantize.zig]\n    \n    N --> S[reference/similarity_ref.zig]\n    P --> T[reference/entities_ref.zig]\n    Q --> U[reference/normalize_ref.zig]\n    R --> V[reference/quantize_ref.zig]\n    \n    style A fill:#e1f5ff\n    style B fill:#fff3cd\n    style E fill:#d4edda\n    style F fill:#d4edda\n    style O fill:#d1ecf1\n    style S fill:#f8d7da\n    style T fill:#f8d7da\n    style U fill:#f8d7da\n    style V fill:#f8d7da\n```\n\n<sub>Last reviewed commit: 1c58e3b</sub>",
